		{
			dependencies: ["70EDF0098A06DF89"]
			description: [
				"&7[NCP Field Memo #0110: Power]"
				""
				"Here's what nobody tells you: GregTech drinks &bEU&r and nothing else. Cheap generators make &bFE&r."
				"They don't speak the same language, and a converter is the only translator."
				"&aThe chain:&r &bsolar panels&r (Solar Flux, 16 FE/t each in daylight, no hull) -> a Powah &bEnergy Cell&r"
				"(it keeps the day for the night) -> a &bULV Energy Converter&r (4 FE make 1 EU; it sets itself to FE to EU"
				"when you place it) -> GregTech cable -> machines."
				"A ULV machine pulls up to 8 EU/t, which is 32 FE/t: two panels per machine while the sun's up,"
				"more if you want the cell full by dark. A &b1A&r converter passes one amp, 8 EU/t at ULV."
				"More machines, more converters (or a 4A one). Panels and cells push into whatever touches them;"
				"Pipez energy pipes carry FE further."
				"&aWhen the sun quits on you:&r the Powah &bFurnator&r burns coal (8 carbon atoms make one)."
				"Panels compact without loss: eight ULV panels and an LV circuit make two LV panels;"
				"from MV up it's four of the last, that tier's circuit and two plates, in an assembler."
				"&7NCP's Emergency Solar (GregTech's ULV panel) puts 8 EU/t straight onto the cable: no converter, no 4:1 loss."
				"&7It costs a hull per panel. There's always a catch."
			]
			id: "37E06DD9764C4021"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 4
					id: "5DB723201558572F"
					item: "positronics:ncp_scrip"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			tasks: [
				{
					count: 2L
					id: "76B77C63AD582FE5"
					item: "solarflux:sp_1"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "718104C01306FD4D"
					item: "gtceu:ulv_1a_energy_converter"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "44F692F393D5939B"
					item: "powah:energy_cell_starter"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Power"
			x: 14.5d
			y: 2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5BF37B5D49C970E6" "37E06DD9764C4021"]
			description: [
				"&7[NCP Field Memo #0111: Machine Shop]"
				""
				"NCP left seven machines for people like you, each good for its own GregTech recipes up to 8 EU/t. Start with these three."
				"The &bCrusher&r turns one stratum into one whole dust. The &bSmelter&r does bronze, red alloy, tin alloy"
				"and &bsteel without a coke oven&r. The &bSifter&r works the trickle while you sleep."
			]
