		}
		{
			dependencies: ["646ADF5E2F61D70F"]
			description: [
				"&7[NCP Field Memo #0117: Metal Atoms]"
				""
				"&bMortar + stratum = 5 atoms&r of its metal. &bMortar + ingot = 16&r. Make sixteen &biron&r and sixteen &bcopper&r:"
				"the tablet you build next will want to learn them."
				"A stratum smelts to 3 nuggets, about 5.3 atoms' worth, so the mortar loses a little. Memory's worth the loss."
				"&bA ring of 8 atoms&r on the crafting table turns back into 4 nuggets (iron, copper, tin, lead, nickel)."
				"&7Flint mortars handle iron and copper; iron-grade mortars add tin, lead and carbon; steel adds nickel."
			]
			id: "271F6CBDB4715876"
